cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this survey, its data or its website, please cite it with the metadata below.
  It is a working draft: it has no DOI and has not been peer-reviewed.
title: "Jev and Typed Decision Models: An Empirical Survey of Calibration, Selective Control, and Open Implementations"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Luo"
    given-names: "Meng"
    website: "https://eurekaleo.github.io/"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Eurekaleo/awesome-jev-survey"
url: "https://eurekaleo.github.io/awesome-jev-survey/"
abstract: >-
  An evidence survey and audit of TypeSafe's Jev and Jev-like typed decision models (data cutoff 2026-09-23):
  13 core studies, 1 peripheral study and 53 background references; 62 claim-level evidence records with
  locators and measurement scope; an openness audit of 30 implementation and evaluation resources; a searchable
  website and a manuscript draft. Values are as reported by their sources; no experiment was re-run.
  Original text, figures and data are licensed CC BY 4.0; the code is MIT-licensed.
keywords:
  - typed decision models
  - Jev
  - calibration
  - selective prediction
  - evidence audit
  - survey
